<crash-analysis>
The crash is caused by a memory leak in the `CleanSpaces` function in `parser.c`.

**Analysis:**
The `CleanSpaces` function allocates a `Stack` object using `TY_(newStack)` on line 555. This stack is used to traverse the HTML node tree. However, the function does not free the allocated stack before it returns. This results in a memory leak every time `CleanSpaces` is called. The crash report shows multiple call stacks leading to `prvTidynewStack`, all of which are part of the normal operation of tidy, and the common factor is the `CleanSpaces` function.

**Suggestion:**
Add a call to `TY_(freeStack)(stack);` at the end of the `CleanSpaces` function, before the final return statement. This will ensure that the allocated stack is properly deallocated, fixing the memory leak.

```c
void TY_(CleanSpaces)( TidyDocImpl* doc, Node *node )
{
Lexer* lexer = doc->lexer;
Node *next;
Stack *stack;

if ( !node )
return;

stack = TY_(newStack)(doc, 32); // 32 is capacity

for (;;)
{
/* ... existing code ... */

for (;;)
{
/* ... existing code ... */

if (node == NULL)
{
TY_(freeStack)(stack); // Add this line
return;
}
}
}
}
```
</crash-analysis>

